<title>FRANCE: French adj March current a/c surplus 9.37 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>French adj March current a/c surplus 9.37 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's current account showed a seasonally adjusted surplus of 9.37 billion francs in March, down from a revised 19.23 billion surplus in February, the Economy Ministry said.</p>
<p>The Ministry said the seasonally adjusted surplus in the first three months of 1997 was 49.6 billion francs, compared with a 31.2 billion surplus in the last quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>Detailed figures in billions of francs showed:</p>
<p>					March     Feb     Jan</p>
<p> Current account (adjusted)    9.37    19.23    21.00</p>
<p> Current account		  14.92    10.42    33.71</p>
<p> Merchandise trade		15.62     9.98     6.65</p>
<p> Services			    7.47     2.00     5.31</p>
<p> Other goods and services	0.00     0.00     0.00</p>
<p> Income			     -4.12     6.09     8.01</p>
<p> Transfers			  -4.05    -7.64    13.73</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
